module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Colimits
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Homology.DerivedCategory.ProjectiveCorepresents
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DerivedTilde.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Duality.CompactGeneration.HomologyDirectSums
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Triangulated.BrownRepresentability

/-!
# Compact generation of the derived category of a ring

[Stacks, Tag 09IS] says that for a quasi-compact, quasi-separated scheme `X` the category
`D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is generated by a single perfect object; over an affine scheme `X = Spec R` the
generator is `𝒪_X` and the source deduces this from the affine comparison
[Stacks, Tag 06Z0] between `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})` and `D(R)`. This file proves the `D(R)` half of
that statement, and in the form Brown representability consumes it.

Let `𝒜` be a Grothendieck abelian category and `P` a projective object of `𝒜` which is compact in
`𝒜`, i.e. `Hom_𝒜(P, -)` commutes with direct sums, and which is a separator, i.e. the only object
receiving only zero maps from `P` is the zero object. Then the complex `P[0]` is a compact
generator of the unbounded derived category `D(𝒜)`: `Hom_{D(𝒜)}(P[0], -)` commutes with direct
sums, and an object of `D(𝒜)` receiving only zero maps from the shifts of `P[0]` is zero.
Consequently every exact functor out of `D(𝒜)` which commutes with direct sums has an exact right
adjoint.

For `𝒜 = ModuleCat R` the object `P = R` satisfies all three conditions, so `D(R)` is compactly
generated by `R[0]` in the sense of [Stacks, Tag 09SQ]. Its compactness is the easy direction of
[Stacks, Tag 07LT] for the particular object `R[0]`.

The two ingredients are `DerivedCategory.homologyFromSingleAddEquiv`, the identification
`Hom_{D(𝒜)}(P[q], Y) ≅ Hom_𝒜(P, Hᑫ(Y))` for `P` projective and `Y` arbitrary, and
`Stacks.Duality.preservesColimitsOfShape_derivedHomologyFunctor`, the fact that the cohomology
functors of `D(𝒜)` commute with direct sums.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Duality.coyonedaSingleIso` — the natural isomorphism
  `Hom_{D(𝒜)}(P[q], -) ≅ Hom_𝒜(P, Hᑫ(-))` of `AddCommGrpCat`-valued functors.
* `Stacks.Duality.preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_singleFunctor_obj` — **a projective compact
  object of `𝒜` gives a compact object `P[q]` of `D(𝒜)`.**
* `Stacks.Duality.isZero_homology_of_forall_hom_single_shift_eq_zero` — a projective separator
  detects cohomology degree by degree: the one shift `P[0]⟦-q⟧` controls `Hᑫ`.
* `Stacks.Duality.isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_single` — **a projective separator of
  `𝒜` gives a generator `P[0]` of `D(𝒜)`**, the previous statement in every degree.
* `Stacks.Duality.exists_isTriangulated_rightAdjoint_of_projectiveSeparator` — Brown
  representability over a Grothendieck abelian category with a compact projective separator.
* `Stacks.Duality.preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_derivedUnit` and
  `Stacks.Duality.isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_derivedUnit` — the two statements for
  `𝒜 = ModuleCat R` and `P = R`.
* `Stacks.Duality.exists_isTriangulated_rightAdjoint_derivedCategoryModuleCat` — **every exact
  functor out of `D(R)` commuting with direct sums has an exact right adjoint.**
* `Stacks.Duality.preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_of_equivalence` and
  `Stacks.Duality.isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_map_of_equivalence` — compactness and
  generation both transfer along an equivalence, which is how the statements above will reach
  `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})` once the affine comparison of [Stacks, Tag 06Z0] is available as an
  equivalence of triangulated categories.

## Implementation notes

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached. Tag 09IS is a statement about `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` for a
quasi-compact, quasi-separated scheme `X`; what is proved here is its algebraic counterpart over
`D(R)`. The affine case of 09IS itself is
`Stacks.Duality.Affine.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_structureSheaf` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Duality/CompactGeneration/AffineGenerator.lean`, which goes through
the equivalence `D(R) ≌ D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})` of [Stacks, Tag 06Z0] — the repository has that
equivalence, as the adjunction `AlgebraicGeometry.derivedTildeQuasicoherentAdjunction` between
`AlgebraicGeometry.derivedTilde` and `AlgebraicGeometry.derivedGlobalSectionsQuasicoherent`
together with the invertibility of its unit and counit. 09IS itself needs in addition the
induction principle of [Stacks, Tag 08DR], the Koszul generators of [Stacks, Tag 09IR], and the
extension of a perfect object from a quasi-compact open, [Stacks, Tag 09IQ], of which the
repository has only the affine case. Tag 07LT is the equivalence of perfectness and compactness
for an arbitrary object of `D(R)`, of which only the compactness of `R[0]` is proved here.

The generating family is the one-element family `fun _ : PUnit => P[0]`, and the shifts are
handled through `CategoryTheory.SingleFunctors.shiftIso`, which identifies `P[0]⟦n⟧` with
`P[-n]`; this is what makes a *single* generator suffice rather than the family of all its
shifts.

The derived category in force is the locally small one — for `ModuleCat R` the instance
`ModuleCat.hasDerivedCategory` puts the morphisms of `D(R)` in the universe of `R` — and not
`HasDerivedCategory.standard`. This is forced rather than chosen: Brown representability needs
direct sums indexed by the types of its own morphism universe, and with the standard model those
are a universe too large to exist in `ModuleCat R`, so the hypotheses of [Stacks, Tag 0A8G] would
be unsatisfiable rather than merely unavailable.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07LT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07LT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09SQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09SQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A8G](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A8G)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06Z0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06Z0)
-/

-- This file uses the locally small derived-category models below, which are not
-- global instances (see `StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedCategory.LocallySmall`):
-- `D(R)` for `R`-modules.
attribute [local instance] ModuleCat.hasDerivedCategory

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty Opposite

universe v u u'

namespace Stacks.Duality

/-! ### Cohomology corepresented by a projective object, as a functor to abelian groups -/

section

variable {𝒜 : Type u} [Category.{v} 𝒜] [Abelian 𝒜] [HasDerivedCategory.{v} 𝒜]

/-- **A projective object corepresents cohomology**, as an isomorphism of
`AddCommGrpCat`-valued functors on the derived category:
`Hom_{D(𝒜)}(P[q], -) ≅ Hom_𝒜(P, Hᑫ(-))`. This is
`DerivedCategory.homologyFromSingleAddEquiv` packaged as a natural isomorphism. -/
def coyonedaSingleIso (P : 𝒜) [Projective P] (q : ℤ) :
    preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor 𝒜 q).obj P)) ≅
      DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor 𝒜 q ⋙ preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op P) :=
  NatIso.ofComponents
    (fun Y => (DerivedCategory.homologyFromSingleAddEquiv P Y q).toAddCommGrpIso)
    fun {_ _} g => by
      ext f
      exact DerivedCategory.homologyFromSingleAddEquiv_comp P _ q f g

end

/-! ### A compact projective object of `𝒜` gives a compact object of `D(𝒜)` -/

section

variable {𝒜 : Type u} [Category.{v} 𝒜] [Abelian 𝒜] [IsGrothendieckAbelian.{v} 𝒜]
  [HasDerivedCategory.{v} 𝒜]

/-- **A projective compact object of `𝒜` gives a compact object of `D(𝒜)`.** If `P` is projective
and `Hom_𝒜(P, -)` commutes with `J`-indexed direct sums, then so does
`Hom_{D(𝒜)}(P[q], -)`: the latter is `Hom_𝒜(P, Hᑫ(-))`, and cohomology commutes with direct
sums. For `𝒜 = ModuleCat R` and `P = R` this is the compactness half of [Stacks, Tag 07LT] for
`R[0]`. -/
theorem preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_singleFunctor_obj (P : 𝒜) [Projective P] (q : ℤ)
    (J : Type v) [PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J) (preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op P))] :
    PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J)
      (preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor 𝒜 q).obj P))) :=
  have := preservesColimitsOfShape_derivedHomologyFunctor 𝒜 (J := J) q
  preservesColimitsOfShape_of_natIso (coyonedaSingleIso P q).symm

/-! ### A projective separator of `𝒜` gives a generator of `D(𝒜)` -/

omit [IsGrothendieckAbelian.{v} 𝒜] in
/-- An object of the derived category whose cohomology vanishes in every degree is zero: the zero
endomorphism is an isomorphism, because it is on every cohomology object. -/
theorem isZero_of_forall_isZero_homology (Y : DerivedCategory 𝒜)
    (h : ∀ q : ℤ, IsZero ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor 𝒜 q).obj Y)) : IsZero Y := by
  have : IsIso (0 : Y ⟶ Y) := by
    rw [DerivedCategory.isIso_iff]
    intro q
    rw [show (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor 𝒜 q).map (0 : Y ⟶ Y) = 𝟙 _ from
      ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor 𝒜 q).map_zero Y Y).trans ((h q).eq_of_src _ _)]
    infer_instance
  rw [IsZero.iff_id_eq_zero]
  have h1 := IsIso.hom_inv_id (0 : Y ⟶ Y)
  rw [zero_comp] at h1
  exact h1.symm

/-- The one-element family consisting of the complex `P[0]`, in the shape in which Brown
representability takes a generating family. -/
def singleGenerator (P : 𝒜) : PUnit.{v + 1} → DerivedCategory 𝒜 :=
  fun _ => (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor 𝒜 0).obj P

/-- The members of `Stacks.Duality.singleGenerator` are compact when `P` is a projective compact
object of `𝒜`, in the shape in which Brown representability takes the hypothesis. -/
theorem preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_singleGenerator (P : 𝒜) [Projective P]
    [∀ J : Type v, PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J) (preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op P))] :
    ∀ (i : PUnit.{v + 1}) (J : Type v), PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J)
      (preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op (singleGenerator P i))) :=
  fun _ J => preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_singleFunctor_obj P 0 J

omit [IsGrothendieckAbelian.{v} 𝒜] in
/-- **A projective separator of `𝒜` detects the cohomology of `D(𝒜)` one degree at a time.** Let
`P` be a projective object of `𝒜` such that the only object receiving only zero morphisms from
`P` is the zero object. If every morphism `P[0]⟦-q⟧ ⟶ Y` vanishes, then `Hᑫ(Y) = 0`.

The shift `P[0]⟦-q⟧` is `P[q]`, and morphisms out of `P[q]` compute `Hom_𝒜(P, Hᑫ(Y))` by
`DerivedCategory.bijective_homologyFromSingle_of_projective`; so the hypothesis says that `Hᑫ(Y)`
receives only zero morphisms from `P`.

One shift controls one cohomology object, and that is the form the truncated Koszul criteria of
[Stacks, Tag 0GEJ] and [Stacks, Tag 0GEK] need: they have the Hom-vanishing on a half-line of
shifts only. `Stacks.Duality.isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_single` is the case of all
shifts at once. -/
theorem isZero_homology_of_forall_hom_single_shift_eq_zero (P : 𝒜) [Projective P]
    (hP : ∀ M : 𝒜, (∀ f : P ⟶ M, f = 0) → IsZero M) (Y : DerivedCategory 𝒜) (q : ℤ)
    (hY : ∀ g : ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor 𝒜 0).obj P)⟦-q⟧ ⟶ Y, g = 0) :
    IsZero ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor 𝒜 q).obj Y) := by
  refine hP _ fun f => ?_
  obtain ⟨g, hg⟩ := (DerivedCategory.bijective_homologyFromSingle_of_projective P Y q).2 f
  have e := ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctors 𝒜).shiftIso (-q) q 0 (by omega)).app P
  have hzero : g = 0 := by
    rw [← cancel_epi e.hom, comp_zero]
    exact hY (e.hom ≫ g)
  rw [← hg, hzero, map_zero]

omit [IsGrothendieckAbelian.{v} 𝒜] in
/-- **A projective separator of `𝒜` generates `D(𝒜)`.** Let `P` be a projective object of `𝒜`
such that the only object of `𝒜` receiving only zero morphisms from `P` is the zero object. If an
object `Y` of `D(𝒜)` receives only zero morphisms from the shifts of `P[0]`, then `Y = 0`: the
shift `P[0]⟦-q⟧` is `P[q]`, morphisms out of it compute `Hom_𝒜(P, Hᑫ(Y))`, so every cohomology
object of `Y` vanishes.

This is `Stacks.Duality.isZero_homology_of_forall_hom_single_shift_eq_zero` in every degree. -/
theorem isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_single (P : 𝒜) [Projective P]
    (hP : ∀ M : 𝒜, (∀ f : P ⟶ M, f = 0) → IsZero M) (Y : DerivedCategory 𝒜)
    (hY : ((ofObj (singleGenerator P)).shiftClosure ℤ).rightOrthogonal Y) :
    IsZero Y :=
  isZero_of_forall_isZero_homology Y fun q =>
    isZero_homology_of_forall_hom_single_shift_eq_zero P hP Y q fun g => hY g
      ⟨(DerivedCategory.singleFunctor 𝒜 0).obj P, -q, Iso.refl _, ofObj_apply _ PUnit.unit⟩

/-- **Brown representability over a Grothendieck abelian category with a compact projective
separator.** Let `𝒜` be a Grothendieck abelian category and `P` a projective object which is
compact (`Hom_𝒜(P, -)` commutes with direct sums) and a separator (only the zero object receives
only zero maps from `P`). Then every exact functor `F : D(𝒜) ⥤ D'` of triangulated categories
which commutes with direct sums has a right adjoint, which is again exact. This is
[Stacks, Tag 0A8G] with its compact-generation hypothesis discharged. -/
theorem exists_isTriangulated_rightAdjoint_of_projectiveSeparator
    {D' : Type u'} [Category.{v} D'] [HasZeroObject D'] [Preadditive D'] [HasShift D' ℤ]
    [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D' n).Additive] [Pretriangulated D']
    (P : 𝒜) [Projective P]
    [∀ J : Type v, PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J) (preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op P))]
    (hP : ∀ M : 𝒜, (∀ f : P ⟶ M, f = 0) → IsZero M)
    (F : DerivedCategory 𝒜 ⥤ D') [F.CommShift ℤ] [F.IsTriangulated]
    [∀ J : Type v, PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J) F] :
    ∃ (G : D' ⥤ DerivedCategory 𝒜) (adj : F ⊣ G) (_ : G.CommShift ℤ), adj.IsTriangulated := by
  have := Stacks.SmallDerivedCategory.hasCoproducts_derivedCategory 𝒜
  have := preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_singleGenerator P
  exact Pretriangulated.exists_isTriangulated_rightAdjoint_of_compactlyGenerated F
    (singleGenerator P) (isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_single P hP)

end

/-! ### Compact generation transfers along an equivalence -/

section

variable {D : Type u} {D' : Type u'} [Category.{v} D] [Category.{v} D'] [Preadditive D]
  [Preadditive D']

/-- **Compactness transfers along an equivalence.** If `e : D ≌ D'` is an equivalence of
preadditive categories whose functor is additive and whose inverse commutes with `J`-indexed
direct sums, then `Hom_{D'}(e.functor.obj K, -)` commutes with `J`-indexed direct sums as soon as
`Hom_D(K, -)` does: the two functors are identified by the hom-set bijection of the adjunction
`e.functor ⊣ e.inverse`.

This is how the compact generators of `D(R)` produced above will reach
`D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec R})` once the affine comparison of [Stacks, Tag 06Z0] is available as an
equivalence of triangulated categories. -/
theorem preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_of_equivalence (e : D ≌ D') [e.functor.Additive]
    (K : D) (J : Type v) [PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J) e.inverse]
    [PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J) (preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op K))] :
    PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J)
      (preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op (e.functor.obj K))) :=
  preservesColimitsOfShape_of_natIso
    (F := e.inverse ⋙ preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op K))
    (NatIso.ofComponents (fun Y => (e.toAdjunction.homAddEquiv K Y).toAddCommGrpIso)
      fun {_ _} g => by
        ext f
        exact e.toAdjunction.homEquiv_naturality_right f g).symm

section Shift

variable [HasShift D ℤ] [HasShift D' ℤ]

/-- **Generation transfers along an equivalence.** Let `e : D ≌ D'` be an equivalence whose
functor is additive and exact for the shifts. If a family `E` generates `D` — the only objects
right orthogonal to all shifts of all `E i` are the zero objects — then the family
`i ↦ e.functor.obj (E i)` generates `D'`.

Together with `Stacks.Duality.preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_of_equivalence` this carries a
compact generating family across an equivalence, which is what turns the statements above about
`D(R)` into the affine case of [Stacks, Tag 09IS] once the comparison of [Stacks, Tag 06Z0] is
available as an equivalence of triangulated categories. -/
theorem isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_map_of_equivalence (e : D ≌ D')
    [e.functor.Additive] [e.functor.CommShift ℤ] {ι : Type*} (E : ι → D)
    (hE : ∀ Y : D, ((ofObj E).shiftClosure ℤ).rightOrthogonal Y → IsZero Y)
    (Y : D') (hY : ((ofObj fun i => e.functor.obj (E i)).shiftClosure ℤ).rightOrthogonal Y) :
    IsZero Y := by
  rw [CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_ofObj_iff] at hY
  have h0 : IsZero (e.inverse.obj Y) := by
    refine hE _
      ((CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_ofObj_iff E _).2
        fun i a f => ?_)
    have hcomp : e.functor.map f ≫ e.counitIso.hom.app Y = 0 := by
      rw [← cancel_epi ((e.functor.commShiftIso a).inv.app (E i)), comp_zero]
      exact hY i a _
    have : e.functor.map f = 0 := by
      rw [← cancel_mono (e.counitIso.hom.app Y), hcomp, zero_comp]
    exact e.functor.map_injective (by rw [this, e.functor.map_zero])
  exact (e.functor.map_isZero h0).of_iso (e.counitIso.app Y).symm

end Shift

end

/-! ### The derived category of a ring -/

section

variable (R : Type u) [Ring R]

/-- `Hom_{ModuleCat R}(R, M)` is `M`: an `R`-linear map out of `R` is its value at `1`. -/
def coyonedaUnitIso :
    preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op (ModuleCat.of R R)) ≅
      forget₂ (ModuleCat.{u} R) AddCommGrpCat.{u} :=
  NatIso.ofComponents
    (fun M => AddEquiv.toAddCommGrpIso
      { toFun := fun f => f.hom (1 : R)
        invFun := fun m => ModuleCat.ofHom (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton R M m)
        left_inv := fun f =>
          ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun r => by
            simpa using (f.hom.map_smul r (1 : R)).symm)
        right_inv := fun m => by simp
        map_add' := fun _ _ => rfl })
    fun {_ _} g => by ext f; rfl

/-- `R` is a separator of `ModuleCat R`: a module receiving only the zero map from `R` is zero,
since an element `m` is the image of `1` under `r ↦ r • m`. -/
theorem isZero_of_forall_hom_unit_eq_zero (M : ModuleCat.{u} R)
    (h : ∀ f : ModuleCat.of R R ⟶ M, f = 0) : IsZero M := by
  rw [ModuleCat.isZero_iff_subsingleton]
  have key : ∀ x : M, x = 0 := fun x => by
    have h0 := ModuleCat.hom_ext_iff.1 (h (ModuleCat.ofHom (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton R M x)))
    simpa using LinearMap.congr_fun h0 (1 : R)
  exact ⟨fun m n => by rw [key m, key n]⟩

/-- `R` is a compact object of `ModuleCat R`: `Hom(R, -)` is the forgetful functor to abelian
groups, which commutes with direct sums. -/
theorem preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_unit (J : Type u) :
    PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J)
      (preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op (ModuleCat.of R R))) :=
  preservesColimitsOfShape_of_natIso (coyonedaUnitIso R).symm

/-- **`R[0]` is a compact object of `D(R)`**: the compactness half of [Stacks, Tag 07LT] for the
unit. -/
theorem preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_derivedUnit (q : ℤ) (J : Type u) :
    PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J)
      (preadditiveCoyoneda.obj
        (op ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} R) q).obj (ModuleCat.of R R)))) :=
  have := preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_unit R J
  preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_singleFunctor_obj _ q J

/-- **`R[0]` generates `D(R)`**: an object of `D(R)` receiving only zero morphisms from the
shifts of `R[0]` is zero. This is the generation half of `D(R)` being compactly generated by
`R[0]`, in the sense of [Stacks, Tag 09SQ]. -/
theorem isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_derivedUnit (Y : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R))
    (hY : ((ofObj (singleGenerator (ModuleCat.of R R))).shiftClosure ℤ).rightOrthogonal Y) :
    IsZero Y :=
  isZero_of_rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_single _ (isZero_of_forall_hom_unit_eq_zero R) Y hY

/-- **Brown representability over `D(R)`.** Every exact functor `F : D(R) ⥤ D'` of triangulated
categories which commutes with direct sums has a right adjoint, which is again exact: `D(R)` is
compactly generated by `R[0]`. This is [Stacks, Tag 0A8G] with its compact-generation hypothesis
discharged, and it is the algebraic counterpart of the affine case of
[Stacks, Tag 09IS]. -/
theorem exists_isTriangulated_rightAdjoint_derivedCategoryModuleCat
    {D' : Type u'} [Category.{u} D'] [HasZeroObject D'] [Preadditive D'] [HasShift D' ℤ]
    [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D' n).Additive] [Pretriangulated D']
    (F : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R) ⥤ D') [F.CommShift ℤ] [F.IsTriangulated]
    [∀ J : Type u, PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J) F] :
    ∃ (G : D' ⥤ DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} R)) (adj : F ⊣ G) (_ : G.CommShift ℤ),
      adj.IsTriangulated :=
  have (J : Type u) : PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete J)
      (preadditiveCoyoneda.obj (op (ModuleCat.of R R))) :=
    preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_unit R J
  exists_isTriangulated_rightAdjoint_of_projectiveSeparator (ModuleCat.of R R)
    (isZero_of_forall_hom_unit_eq_zero R) F

end

end Stacks.Duality

end
